.SH NAME
anpu-show - Open the results of a past scan


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu show  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a stored scan from the local history database
(~/.anpu/anpu.db) — the same record \fBanpu diff\fR compares.

.PP
Findings can be filtered by severity floor (--severity) and capped
(--limit, 0 = all). --long adds full finding IDs (for --risk-accept
files), URLs, and evidence excerpts.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--export\fP=""
	re-render this scan to a file instead of printing a summary

.PP
\fB--format\fP="html"
	export format when --export is set: html, json, sarif, csv, md, junit

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for show

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	max findings to print (0 = all)

.PP
\fB--long\fP[=false]
	print full finding IDs, URLs, and evidence excerpts

.PP
\fB--severity\fP=""
	minimum severity to print: low, medium, high, critical (empty = all)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


